  "coord": "27:7",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "invention",
  "note": "\"a statue\" is not in the source (\"a thing made for Alexander\").",
  "replacement": "MENENIUS. So he did me, and he remembers his mother no more now than an eight-year-old horse does. The sourness of his face turns ripe grapes sour. When he walks, he moves like a siege engine, and the ground shrinks under his tread. He can pierce a breastplate with his eye, talks like a funeral bell, and his hum is a cannonade. He sits on his throne like something made for Alexander. What he orders to be done is finished as soon as he orders it. He lacks nothing of a god but eternity and a heaven to sit enthroned in."
 },
